  m_Name: Debrief_M4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: LastSignal.Core::LastSignal.DebriefCard
  title: "Someone's Been Living Here"
  concept: "Landing-site selection and exoplanet characterisation"
  nasaSource: "NASA Exoplanet Archive (radius, insolation, equilibrium temperature, orbital period); NASA/JPL Mars 2020 landing-site selection and Terrain-Relative Navigation"
  body: "Mission planners rank landing sites by slope, boulders, sunlight for power and science value such as water. Perseverance used Terrain-Relative Navigation to steer away from hazards while landing in Jezero Crater. The planet you scanned is built from real measurements in the NASA Exoplanet Archive: its radius hints at a rocky world, and the starlight it receives sets its equilibrium temperature. Landing limits, fuel and power in this mission are game-balance values."
